{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ba043205e1d610092540a22902fc635f77b826f3ce3fc1abcd944f6f60b2e568","digest":{"component_or_area":"llm-framework accounting documentation","key_entities":["docs/llm-framework.md","runner_support._intersect_capabilities","src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py","rebar.toml","prompt_cache_style","cache_read_tokens","cache_write_tokens"],"problem_keywords":["prompt caching","fallback chain","mixed-provider","capability intersection","accounting documentation","cache disabled"],"propositions":["A mixed-provider fallback chain disables prompt caching by design because provider-specific cache keys do not intersect across candidates.","The accounting section of docs/llm-framework.md does not document that fallback chains collapse disagreeing prompt_cache_style values to 'none', leaving operators unable to reconcile zero cache counts against single-model behavior.","An operator observing zero cache read/write tokens on a chain-backed operation must understand this reflects the conservative capability intersection, not a regression.","The runtime behavior and intersection logic are already implemented correctly in runner_support._intersect_capabilities and documented in rebar.toml, but the operator-facing accounting contract is incomplete."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787606047012539001,"uuid":"c1222831-38ba-4ca4-8f4a-30c9e82f74e4"}